# The docked turn checklist (play/TurnPanel) on a six-timeline Standard game: White to move at T5w, five boards to move on (L+3, L+2, L+1,
# L-1, L-2) and L0, which is ahead. The panel is 300 px wide at the right; its rows are 48 px from y=112 (row n's middle: y = 136 + 48 n),
# so a row is clicked at x=1200.
record ../records/many-boards.5dr
wait 150
capture checklist-start

# Three of the five boards played: ticked rows keep their place and name their move; the pill and the header say 3 / 5; Submit stays locked
clicksq 3 8 d1
wait 40
clicksq 3 8 b3
wait 60
clicksq 2 8 b1
wait 40
clicksq 2 8 a3
wait 60
clicksq 1 8 d2
wait 40
clicksq 1 8 d4
wait 60
key HOME
wait 40
capture checklist-three-of-five

# The pointer on a row rings its board in the multiverse (the L-1 row)
move 1200 280
wait 12
capture checklist-hover-row

# L-2's queen jumps to L-1: both rows are done at once ("queen arrived from L-2"), Submit is ready
clicksq -2 8 d1
wait 40
# (the target board is above the view: drag it into sight so no ghost tag covers c2)
drag 300 300 300 560 6
wait 30
hoversq -1 8 c2
wait 30
clicksq -1 8 c2
wait 80
key HOME
wait 40
capture checklist-ready

# Undo takes the last move back and the rows with it
key U
wait 40
capture checklist-undo

# A click on a row shows that board (Focus)
click 1200 280
wait 60
capture checklist-row-focus
